decisions:
  - id: d-roster-14
    decision: '14-agent roster for paradigm: core 8 + dx, release, debugger, qa, educator, researcher, performance, designer'
    rationale: Dev tools monorepo needs DX, release, and education specialists over sales/SEO/DBA agents
  - id: d-toolregistry-wired
    decision: Wire existing ToolRegistry into actual MCP dispatch path
    rationale: Built but unused architecture — highest ROI refactor. Cuts tool count from 176 to ~50-80 per project, O(1) dispatch
  - id: d-compliance-consolidate
    decision: Single paradigm compliance-check command replaces 5 stop-hook subprocesses
    rationale: 5 Node.js spawns + 2 find scans per session end was 1-2 seconds overhead
  - id: d-conductor-environment
    decision: Replace 15 @ObservedObject with single ConductorEnvironment @EnvironmentObject
    rationale: God-view anti-pattern made refactoring fragile and caused unnecessary re-renders
  - id: d-css-unification
    decision: Migrate Lore/Graph CSS to Platform --p-* token system
    rationale: Three competing :root declarations were overriding each other order-dependently
  - id: d-ripple-standalone
    decision: Extract paradigm_ripple from preflight into standalone core-tier MCP tool
    rationale: Referenced everywhere but didn't exist as real tool. Hardcoded 2-hop was insufficient
  - id: d-portal-dogfood
    decision: Expand portal.yaml from 1 gate/6 routes to 4 gates/94 routes
    rationale: Paradigm must eat its own cooking — flagship security feature had token coverage
learnings:
  - Builder subagents get blocked on Write/Bash permissions — use general-purpose agents or do edits directly
  - 'ToolRegistry was the single highest-ROI refactor: built, tested, but never wired in'
  - Review agents read extensively but don't always synthesize — budget for a follow-up synthesis prompt
  - 4 parallel agents with zero file overlap is the sweet spot for this codebase
  - Plugin version in plugin.json STILL gets missed — added to every commit checklist
