body: |-
  ## Session Arc

  This session began with recovering the handoff from the v5.6.3–v5.11.0 marathon and evolved into a systematic polish sprint.

  ### Phase 1: Agent Setup
  Registered a 14-agent roster for the paradigm repo itself and bootstrapped 29 project-scoped notebook entries covering architecture, build chain, testing, security, DX, release, debugging, QA, education, research, performance, and design.

  ### Phase 2: Team Review
  Deployed 5 review agents in parallel: Architecture+Code Quality, Conductor UI/UX (Mika), Platform UI (Mika), University (Educator), Performance+DX (Bolt+Helix). Produced 100+ findings across the codebase. The architecture agent read extensively but didn't synthesize — had to launch a replacement.

  ### Phase 3: Quick Fixes (v5.12.0)
  Platform UI: URL routing for all 11 sections, ErrorBoundary per section, removed duplicate theme toggle. Conductor: ConductorColors.swift, dynamic version, window mode persistence. CLI: lazy-load init/status, treeshake+minify on 5 tsup configs. University: fixed stale .purpose files.

  ### Phase 4: Architecture (v5.13.0)
  ToolRegistry wired into actual MCP dispatch (176 tools in 3 tiers). compliance-check command (5→1 subprocess). ConductorTheme design tokens. ConductorEnvironment (15→1 @ObservedObject). A11y labels on all status dots. Unified CSS tokens. Shared Platform components.

  ### Phase 5: DX Polish (v5.14.0)
  Command palette (Cmd+K). paradigm explain-files command. cli-output.ts convention with 3 example conversions.

  ### Phase 6: Core Framework (v5.15.0)
  paradigm_ripple as standalone MCP tool with BFS depth control. Portal eat-our-own-cooking (1→4 gates, 6→94 routes). All 57 .purpose files standardized to v2.0.0. Drift auto-heal thresholds documented and configurable.

  ## What's Next
  Section 2 of the polish checklist: Agent System. Then continue through all 18 sections.
